 equal-area two-factor reduction and smooth genus-one cuts","audit_proof_section":"A,C","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"The integer condition 4d divides K requires integral d; rational d uses actual root denominators."},{"id":"O2","claim":"Correct cover multiplicity and squareclass inverse","audit_proof_section":"C","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"Binding RETURN correction supersedes the unrestricted four-lift wording on the positive-d slice. No inverse statement at v=0."},{"id":"O3","claim":"All odd multiples on fixed equal-area core yield cuts","audit_proof_section":"C","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"Finite rows are regression only; no uniform classification of all equal-area cores."},{"id":"O4","claim":"Exact denominator, parity, sixteen-root primitive gcd and injective family","audit_proof_section":"C","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"Artificial parity inputs are not curve points; v2(p)>=3 requires extra factor two; no six-coordinate-gcd substitution."},{"id":"O5","claim":"Fixed-core zero-column classification and n>=3 avoidance","audit_proof_section":"C","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"Classification applies to this fixed core only, not all off-diagonal equal-area fibers."},{"id":"I1","claim":"Common interface compatibility with separate coordinate layers","audit_proof_section":"D","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"Does not extend K!=0 theorem over K=0, identify xi with u, or identify branches by undocumented quotient."},{"id":"I2","claim":"Observer-safe primitive quotient and operation horizon","audit_proof_section":"D","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"Bare unsigned outputs do not support arbitrary future elliptic addition; scale quotient is not equality of unscaled roots."},{"id":"T1","claim":"External arithmetic remains separated from native P000 X6","audit_proof_section":"D","status":"VERIFIED_COMPATIBLE","boundary":"No native plane, 90-degree geometry, continuous/fractional Cell moti